---
alwaysApply: true
description: During Q&A, answer questions without editing code or taking unrelated actions; code changes require explicit instruction
---
### Q&A behavior: answer without editing code

- When the user asks a question, answer the question directly. Do not modify code as part of the answer, even if issues are discovered while answering.
- Do not execute unrelated tasks or actions after answering. Keep responses scoped strictly to the question.

### Code changes require explicit instruction

- Do not modify code unless the user explicitly requests an edit or change.
- If a potential problem is identified while answering, present a brief analysis and request confirmation before any edit (see `confirm-on-concerns.mdc`).

### Conversation scope

- Do not proactively modify code not mentioned in the conversation, even if it appears in a pending TODO list.
- Follow `todo-confirmation.mdc` before proposing or committing any TODO list.

### Related rules

- `wait-for-review.mdc` — do not self-start new tasks after completing current work.
- `stop-after-each-unit.mdc` — pause after each discrete unit for review.
- `edit-explanation.mdc` — include concise rationale when edits are explicitly requested and made.
